    "['mpls te tunnel-id [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'tunnel mpls traffic-eng 100', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'For the HUAWEI command `mpls te tunnel-id 100`, the equivalent Cisco IOS XR command would be:\\n\\n##\\ntunnel mpls traffic-eng 100\\n##\\n\\nOr for Cisco IOS (non-XR), it would typically be:\\n\\n##\\ntunnel mpls traffic-eng tunnel-id 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact command may vary slightly depending on Cisco platform and software version. The key is that both configure the MPLS TE tunnel with ID 100.', 'trans_template': 'tunnel mpls traffic-eng 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'tunnel mpls traffic-eng tunnel-id 100', 'parent_command': ['interface [parameter1]'], 'root': 'interface [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'For the HUAWEI command `mpls te tunnel-id 100`, the equivalent Cisco IOS XR command would be:\\n\\n##\\ntunnel mpls traffic-eng 100\\n##\\n\\nOr for Cisco IOS (non-XR), it would typically be:\\n\\n##\\ntunnel mpls traffic-eng tunnel-id 100\\n##\\n\\nNote: The exact command may vary slightly depending on Cisco platform and software version. The key is that both configure the MPLS TE tunnel with ID 100.', 'trans_template': 'tunnel mpls traffic-eng tunnel-id 100'}]]": 1,
